00:33:43,190 --> 00:33:46,549
people are not really going to do it unless they understand why.

511
00:33:46,559 --> 00:33:48,790
you need to sell them on that. absolutely.

512
00:33:48,799 --> 00:33:52,870
i had a cto very early in my career. and he told me something that stuck with me forever.

513
00:33:52,880 --> 00:33:55,750
he's like, jeff, you know, when we're making big changes.

514
00:33:55,760 --> 00:34:01,269
the order is people, process, tools.

515
00:34:01,269 --> 00:34:03,029
you have to win, you have to implement in that order.

516
00:34:03,039 --> 00:34:06,310
you've got to get the people on board with what it is you're trying to do.

517
00:34:06,320 --> 00:34:10,389
you've got to define the process that you're going to follow.

518
00:34:10,399 --> 00:34:14,149
then you find the tools that are going to implement that process.

519
00:34:14,159 --> 00:34:18,230
and so often we sort of start at the end of that, right?

520
00:34:18,230 --> 00:34:23,030
we pick a tool, and then we define, oh, okay, yeah, now that we've got kubernetes. this is the process that we're going to follow.

521
00:34:23,040 --> 00:34:25,669
and now that we've got the process defined.

522
00:34:25,669 --> 00:34:30,311
we're going to go tell the engineers, hey, you're going to be on call for the rest of your life now, right? and that doesn't work.

523
00:34:30,311 --> 00:34:36,950
because, you know, from an engineering perspective is change is happening to you, right? not with you, it's happening to you.

524
00:34:36,960 --> 00:34:40,869
so you know, that order of things is very important.

525
00:34:40,869 --> 00:34:43,990
and then once you have the people on board, and you've got the process defined.

526
00:34:44,000 --> 00:34:47,190
picking a tool becomes a lot easier, right?

527
00:34:47,190 --> 00:34:49,190
because you know what it is you're trying to accomplish.

528
00:34:49,200 --> 00:34:52,550
so when it doesn't have this whispy feature.

529
00:34:52,550 --> 00:34:54,470
you're like, well, it doesn't really matter.

530
00:34:54,470 --> 00:34:57,030
because that's not the process that we're going to follow. so we don't care.

531
00:34:57,040 --> 00:35:01,990
so it really empowers you in a way to make better decisions.

532
00:35:01,990 --> 00:35:03,510
about the technology choices you have.

533
00:35:03,520 --> 00:35:07,990
jeff, let's move on and address another topic.

