00:39:01,839 --> 00:39:05,510
versus, you know, login page loads are extremely slow.

599
00:39:05,520 --> 00:39:07,589
correlated with high cpu utilization.

600
00:39:07,599 --> 00:39:11,589
it's like, oh, okay, now there's an actual user impact that i understand.

601
00:39:11,599 --> 00:39:15,030
and i know that this is related to high cpu utilization.

602
00:39:15,040 --> 00:39:17,910
i think one of the things that has been sort of an eye opener.

603
00:39:17,910 --> 00:39:20,790
is when people realize, or at least old people realize.

604
00:39:20,790 --> 00:39:26,471
that we're not bound to character text message sizes anymore, right? so i remember when i first started.

605
00:39:26,480 --> 00:39:29,990
when you had to write an alert that would page.

